"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwoodpecker=self.webpackChunkwoodpecker||[]).push([["7873"],{64657(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"name":"Mastodon Post","slug":"mastodon-post","url":"https://codeberg.org/woodpecker-plugins/mastodon-post","icon":"https://joinmastodon.org/logos/logo-purple.svg","description":"Post statuses to Mastodon.","docs":"<h1>Mastodon Post plugin</h1>\\n<p>Woodpecker plugin to post statuses to Mastodon.</p>\\n<h2>Usage</h2>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-yaml\\">image: woodpeckerci/plugin-mastodon-post\\nsettings:\\n  server_url: https://mastodon.social\\n  access_token:\\n    from_secret: your_access_token\\n  status: We just released {{ CI_COMMIT_TAG }} \u{1F680}\\n</code></pre>\\n<h3>Settings</h3>\\n<table>\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>Settings Name</th>\\n<th>Default</th>\\n<th>Description</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody><tr>\\n<td><code>server_url</code></td>\\n<td><em>none</em></td>\\n<td><strong>Required.</strong> Mastodon server url, including protocol.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>access_token</code></td>\\n<td><em>none</em></td>\\n<td><strong>Required.</strong> Mastodon access token. (<a href=\\"#get-access-token\\">How to get Token</a>)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>status</code></td>\\n<td><em>none</em></td>\\n<td><strong>Required</strong> (if <code>ai_token</code> is not set). Status message (Allows <a href=\\"#templating\\">Templating</a>)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>sensitive</code></td>\\n<td><code>false</code></td>\\n<td>Mark post as sensitive (<code>true</code> or <code>false</code>)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>files</code></td>\\n<td><em>none</em></td>\\n<td><code>,</code>-separated paths or globs of images, videos or audio files, see <a href=\\"#media\\">Media</a></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>media</code></td>\\n<td><em>none</em></td>\\n<td><code>{ path, alt, focus, thumbnail }</code> list, instead of <code>files</code>, see <a href=\\"#media\\">Media</a></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>in_reply_to_id</code></td>\\n<td><em>none</em></td>\\n<td>ID of post to reply to</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>spoiler_text</code></td>\\n<td><em>none</em></td>\\n<td>Spoiler text</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>visibility</code></td>\\n<td><code>null</code></td>\\n<td>Visibility (<code>private</code>, <code>unlisted</code>, <code>public</code> or <code>direct</code>)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>language</code></td>\\n<td><em>none</em></td>\\n<td>Status language</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>ai_token</code></td>\\n<td><em>none</em></td>\\n<td><strong>Required</strong> (if <code>status</code> is not set). Provide an AI token (OpenAI) to generate a status message</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>ai_model</code></td>\\n<td><code>gpt-5-nano</code></td>\\n<td>Select the model used to generate a status message</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>ai_url</code></td>\\n<td>OpenAI</td>\\n<td>Base URL of an OpenAI compatible API, e.g. <a href=\\"#self-hosted-models\\">Ollama</a></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>ai_prompt</code></td>\\n<td><a href=\\"#default-ai-prompt\\">prompt</a></td>\\n<td>Prompt used to generate a status message. (Allows <a href=\\"#templating\\">Templating</a>)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>changelog_file</code></td>\\n<td><code>CHANGELOG.md</code></td>\\n<td>File to use for the AI to make a changelog from.</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody></table>\\n<h3>Get Access Token</h3>\\n<p>In order to get an access token, open your Settings and go to the <code>Development</code> section. There create a new application and make sure that <code>write:statuses</code> is checked (Also requires <code>write:media</code> when using the <code>files</code> or <code>media</code> setting).<br>After creating your application, copy the text next to <code>Your access token</code> and use that as your <code>access_token</code> value.</p>\\n<h3>Media</h3>\\n<p><code>files</code> attaches images, videos or audio files. Entries can be paths or globs like <code>dist/*.png</code>, and the path of each\\nfile is used as its alt text.</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-yaml\\">settings:\\n  files:\\n    - dist/screenshot.png\\n    - docs/release/*.png\\n</code></pre>\\n<p>To set your own alt texts, use <code>media</code> instead of <code>files</code>. Each entry needs a <code>path</code>, globs are not supported. The <code>alt</code>\\ntext allows <a href=\\"#templating\\">Templating</a>, and without it the path is used. Set <code>alt: \\"\\"</code> for purely decorative images.</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><code>focus</code> sets the focal point of an image as <code>x,y</code>, each from -1 to 1: <code>0,0</code> is the center, <code>-1,1</code> the top left\\ncorner. Apps keep it visible when they crop the preview.</li>\\n<li><code>thumbnail</code> sets a custom preview image for a video or audio file, such as a poster frame or cover art.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-yaml\\">settings:\\n  media:\\n    - path: dist/screenshot.png\\n      alt: The new dashboard, released in {{ CI_COMMIT_TAG }}\\n      focus: 0,0.8\\n    - path: dist/logo.png\\n      alt: \'\'\\n</code></pre>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-yaml\\">settings:\\n  media:\\n    - path: dist/demo.mp4\\n      alt: A 30 second tour of the new dashboard\\n      thumbnail: dist/demo-poster.png\\n</code></pre>\\n<p>A status can have up to 4 images, or one video or audio file. By default Mastodon accepts JPEG, PNG, GIF and WebP\\nimages (HEIC, HEIF and AVIF on some servers) of up to 16 MiB, and MP4, WebM, MOV or Ogg videos and MP3, Ogg, WAV, FLAC,\\nAAC or M4A audio files of up to 99 MiB. The plugin reads the actual limits of your server and checks every file before\\nanything is posted, reporting all problems at once. Set <code>sensitive: true</code> or a <code>spoiler_text</code> to hide the media behind a\\nwarning.</p>\\n<p>Files are uploaded before the status is posted. Mastodon processes videos and audio after the upload, and the plugin\\nwaits up to 5 minutes for that to finish. If an upload or the status fails, the files uploaded so far are deleted again.</p>\\n<h3>Templating</h3>\\n<p>You can use <code>{{ CI_COMMIT_TAG }}</code> and other environment variables in the <code>status</code> and <code>ai_prompt</code> settings and in <code>alt</code> texts of <code>media</code>.\\nThe <code>ai_prompt</code> template can also use <code>{{ CHANGELOG }}</code> to include the changelog of the release.\\nThe <code>access_token</code> and <code>ai_token</code> values are never available as placeholders, and AI generated text is posted as is.</p>\\n<h3>Self-hosted models</h3>\\n<p>Any server with an OpenAI compatible <code>chat/completions</code> endpoint works, for example <a href=\\"https://ollama.com\\">Ollama</a>.\\n<code>ai_token</code> still enables the AI and is sent as bearer token; a local Ollama ignores it, so any value will do.</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-yaml\\">image: woodpeckerci/plugin-mastodon-post\\nsettings:\\n  server_url: https://mastodon.social\\n  access_token:\\n    from_secret: your_access_token\\n  ai_url: http://ollama:11434/v1\\n  ai_token: unused\\n  ai_model: llama3.2\\n</code></pre>\\n<h3>Default AI prompt</h3>\\n<p>Used when <code>ai_prompt</code> is not set. Copy of the prompt defined in <a href=\\"https://codeberg.org/woodpecker-plugins/mastodon-post/src/branch/main/src/utils.ts\\"><code>src/utils.ts</code></a>:</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-text\\">We want to announce the next version of our app on Mastodon.\\nWrite a catchy post, so users will know why they should update to the newest\\nversion. If there is no special feature included, just summarize the changes\\nin a few sentences. Reply with the post text only, at most 500 characters long.\\n\\nThe changelog entry: {{ changelog }}\\n</code></pre>\\n","tags":["post","status","mastodon"],"containerImage":"woodpeckerci/plugin-mastodon-post","containerImageUrl":"https://hub.docker.com/r/woodpeckerci/plugin-mastodon-post","verified":true,"iconDataUrl":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,"}')}}]);